  "Frederick Douglass. Taught himself to read when it was forbidden to him, escaped slavery at twenty, and wrote it all down for the world to answer for.": [
   795440,
   7445
  ],
  "Harriet Tubman. She got herself free — then went back some thirteen times for family and strangers alike, and she brought out every single one.": [
   803135,
   7955
  ],
  "Nat Turner. In 1831 he rose in Southampton County and led the deadliest slave rebellion in American history.": [
   811340,
   7220
  ],
  "Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Twenty-six years old when Montgomery stopped riding the buses — and he led that boycott all 381 days.": [
   818810,
   7540
  ],
  "Sojourner Truth. Born enslaved — and the first Black woman to win a court case against a white man in this country, bringing her own son home.": [
   826600,
